# Career Agent: environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` if you need it. `.env` is gitignored and must never
# be committed.
#
#   Windows:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   macOS / Linux:  cp .env.example .env
#
# YOU ALMOST CERTAINLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.
#
# The product is local-first. Collecting postings, deduplicating them, scoring
# them, filtering them, tracking applications and running the local AI summaries
# all work with no `.env` present at all. There is no account, no billing and no
# hosted model in the path of anything you can see in the interface.
#
# Nothing below is a real value. Placeholders only.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_API_KEY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What it is for:
#   The PAUSED hosted-model qualification programme, and nothing else. That
#   work asked whether a hosted model could produce an evidence-grounded
#   JobFingerprint that survives the evidence validator. It was paused when the
#   deterministic local product shipped (ADR-0010, marker
#   HOSTED_MODEL_QUALIFICATION_PAUSED_FOR_PRODUCT_PIVOT), and it is preserved
#   rather than deleted.
#
# What reads it:
#   Only `career-agent run-extraction`, and only when you pass `--execute`
#   together with an explicit `--db`, an explicit selection and an explicit
#   `--max-live-calls` (ADR-0009). Without `--execute` that command constructs
#   no client, reads no credential value and makes no request. `doctor` reports
#   this variable as PRESENT or MISSING and never prints its value.
#
# What does NOT read it:
#   Everything you would call the product. `collect`, `collect-speedrun`,
#   `import-job`, `rescore`, `serve`, `enrich`, `ollama-check`, `seed-demo`,
#   `search-config` and `coverage-report` never look at it. The local Ollama
#   client refuses any non-loopback address and has no API-key concept at all.
#
# A configured key is never authorisation. Setting this variable does not make
# any command call a vendor.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY is accepted as an alternative name; the Google SDK prefers
# GOOGLE_API_KEY. Set one, not both.
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-key-here


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not credentials, and not required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are ordinary settings rather than secrets. They are listed here so that
# nobody has to go looking for them in the source. Each one has a working
# default and the product runs correctly with all of them unset.
#
# CAREER_AGENT_DB    Absolute path to your personal database, so you can stop
#                    passing `--db` to every command. An explicit `--db` still
#                    wins. Demo mode ignores this entirely.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL    Where the LOCAL model listens. Default
#                    http://localhost:11434. A non-loopback address is refused
#                    before any request is built, without resolving DNS.
# OLLAMA_MODEL       Default qwen3:4b.
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS  Default 300000, which is five minutes. A small model on
#                    CPU is slow rather than broken.
#
# There is deliberately no OLLAMA_API_KEY. Loopback needs no authentication and
# nothing here would read one.
#
# CAREER_AGENT_DB=/absolute/path/to/career.db
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:4b
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
